That bad?  The 21164 is an ancient processor.  A box with a 21164/300
was available in January *1996* (source: spec newsletter 2/96).
It delivered 8.02 SPECint95 in an AS2100A.

The 21164A (a shrink of the 21164 with a few instructions added,
same L1/L2 cache size) reached 16.7 SPECint95 at 533 MHz in an AS4100,
available in October 1997, and 15.0 SPECint95 at 500 MHz in an AS500/500,
available in October 1996*

No surprise that now, two and a half years after the 21164A/500,
a PIII/500 is faster.

Unfortunately the 21264 (26.9 SPECint95 in an XP1000 at 500 MHz)
came out much too late, it's still quite new and rather expensive.

joerch (proud owner of a prehistoric 21066A/233 and an ancient 21164A/500) :-)



