On Tue, 20 Apr 1999 12:01:22 +0100, Nathan McEachen
<nmceache@hornet.csc.calpoly.edu> wrote: 
>Is it possible to install both KDE and GNOME, and then switch easily
>between the two?  Can I run KDE one minute, and then change my mind
>and decide to run GNOME the next?

KDE and GNOME represent:
a) A set of application libraries to help construct applications, and
b) A set of applications written using these libraries.

The libraries use distinct names, as do the applications, and have
distinct "namespaces."

It should be manifestly obvious from the above that applications written
for KDE and GNOME can co-exist simultaneously.
