I can run both ARC (AlphaBIOS) and SRM on may AlphaStation 200.  The
firmware is stored in flash memory, and updates are available from the 
Digital web site.  I think that all the newer Alphas have flash memory
for the firmware.

Either ARC or SRM can boot Linux, but I think ARC is needed to boot 
NT.  I don't know if ARC can boot OSF1/Digital Unix/Tru64.  

More information on booting Alpha Linux can be found at 
http://www.alphalinux.org/faq/FAQ-16.html.

