From a discussion of GCC design, it does not at all follow that
"They might as well put the compiler front-ends and GEM into the
public domain."  If DEC had some magical technique inside their
compiler, making it public would allow Sun to use it in SPARC
compilers, HP to use it in Merced<DEL><DEL><DEL><DEL><DEL><DEL>
compilers for their machines, etc.

DEC's interest would be in having GCC do very well on Alpha,
and I recall seeing Web documents on how to schedule Alpha
instructions in your own compiler.  Perhaps they have fewer
people assigned to this writing chore than they should, but
releasing Alpha tips is quite different from releasing their
compiler designs.

Larry



