  "Anthony J. Gabrielson" <agabriel@coe.neu.edu> wrote:
> I recently put RH 5.2 on an Alpha Multia.  The machine runs very nice.
> However, there are several files that a edited in /etc and it insists on
> changing it back to the preedited state.  First it happened w\ hosts -
> found I have to use there tool to make it work.  Now its w\ issue
> & issue.net.  If any one knows what utility I can use - or what utility
> needs to be disabled, it would be greatly appreciated.


These files are created by the bootime script:
/etc/rc.d/rc.local

To have custom versions modify this script.
Note: This is a actually a security issue because the .issue and .issue should
give no information about the machine or the OS. It helps crackers to much.

You can safely edit /etc/hosts at the command line and the changes will remain
in the file. If you have the control_panel editor up at the same time though
it will overwrite the file.

Hope this helps.

