You don't need to upgrade.
DNS gives a minor load on your system. SMTP gives a minor load (except
with huge maillists) and POP3 is very nice to your resources asswell.
When you would run EXCHANGE then you needed to upgrade ;-)
You should take care that the people will only check their mailbox every
20 or 30 minutes evry 5 would be much and your network would choke
(except if you have TokenRing or 100MB/s eth)

What I would do is to add a other harddrive and set the mqueue on that
drive. Since 1 GB is pretty small for 250 people their mailbox.

We run a P133 for only 32 users and it does Intranet, SMTP, POP3, SQUID
Proxy, DNS, Masquerading and Database (MySQL) and our avg load is 0.1
but no-one complains except for bandwidth on the internet ;-)

Raymond


