This provides a really, really good argument for making the kernel more
modular, of course - because, assuming DECC is significantly better than
gcc and that most users won't have DECC, you'll get quite a performance
hit by being forced to recompile the kernel, since the one you'll have
been shipped will have been produced by Redhat or Debian or whoever
using DECC.

Tom




