Paul DeMone <pdemone@igs.net> writes:

>   DEC probably has the best binary recompilation and object code
>   optimization technology in the business.  If it really wanted
>   to keep its algorithms under wraps it could just release a GCC
>   output optimizer as an executable.  Ugly but better than nothing.

As I understand it, that wouldn't work: GCC's intermedaite representation
is outdated and isn't able to convey enough of the information required for
many modern optimization techniques. Look at the struggle the g77 people
are having in trying to get the GCC backend use the additional semantics
a language such as Fortran can provide to the compiler (e.g., regarding
aliasing).

	Jan



