It seems that the negative comments about Compaq's decision not to
provide the source for their Fortran compiler for free are not
coming from Fortran programmers.  The open source software folks are
nowhere near producing an optimizer that is as good as Compaq's,
even though Compaq's optimizer has, in my view, some shortcomings.
Nobody has yet produced an open source Fortran compiler on any
platform AFAIK (g77 is not a Fortran compiler).  There is no
question that Compaq's product is better that any open source
compiler; something is better than nothing.  Of course that point
is not yet valid on Alpha Linux but it is on Alpha NT.





