>
> > >>>boot vda -file vmlinux.gz -flags "root=/dev/fd0 loadramdisk=1
> > promptramdisk=1"
>
> load_ramdisk has an underscore in it.
>
> prompt_ramdisk is no longer necessary.
>
> -flags "root=/dev/fd0 load_ramdisk=1"
>
> -- g

Thanks. There is no difference between loadramdisk and load_ramdisk.
Anyway it doesn't work :-(

I found the workaround:

1. Prepare new boot kernel (2.2.3) diskette (get it from www.alphalinux.org)
2. Download ramdisk image from the distribution.
3. Gunzip ramdisk image
4. dd ramdisk image into hdd partition
5. boot the box from the new diskette with root=/dev/sdxx statement
6. go with the installation

The procedure above works with debian. It works with redhat 5.2 also,
but redhat for alpha has a bug:
if you try to perform ftp installation (I have no CD with alpha distribution)
you cannot setup network card ('SCIOADDRT: file exist' message) -- DS20
has tulip NIC.

So now I'm playing with dselect -- the most misterious package manager
I ever seen... ;-)

best regards, Janusz


