I suspect that a move from GCC to "CCC" (Compaq C Compiler? :-)) is
not likely to take place any time soon, certainly in part for the
reason that it would *probably* require that the Linux/Alpha kernel
diverge from the "normal" kernel base.  

The hue and cry that *that* would cause would be *rather* hurtful.

I would think that much greater benefits would come from recompiling
GLIBC, which would doubtless be much less controversial.

