Michael Tin wrote:
> 
> Well, I'm trying to setup my alpha box as a server, and it used to boot
> fine. Until I tried to access my cable modem through my hub. When it
> gets to sendmail, it just hangs. I reinstalled linux but it still does
> it. It didnt use to. Maybe it was my network config, I dont know. The
> info Comcast@home gave me was really weird like the host name was like
> ccXXXXX-b where XXXXX are numbers. Then the domain name was like
> nwbch.occa.home.com Now I'm not a networker by any means but they just
> dont sound right. When I reinstalled linux to take advantage of these
> things(cable modem), it suddenly hangs at sendmail. But I have enough
> control to reboot and stuff like that(CTRL-ALT-DEL still restarts the
> computer). Maybe it is because of my ethernet card. I got this cheap
> intel etherexpress pro 100, but it would refuse to talk to the cable
> modem. I got one for my wintel machine too, but even that wouldnt work.
> so I am stuck.
> I had to get another card(from comcast) and that worked. I am not sure
> what is going on here so any help would be appreciated.
> Thanks,
> Mike Tin
> qaa@mailcity.com

There is a problem with your network connection or DNS name resolution.
sendmail tries to map your hostname to an IP number (or the other way
around, I forget which) and hangs while waiting for the DNS query to
complete. You should boot to single-user mode, disable sendmail and try
to resolve all DNS/network problems you have.

-Mikko Hyvarinen



