There are native Alpha Amaya rpm's around of V 1.3a: since my machine 
was busted (actually, it died, and was replaced) for a while (on which 
they were built) Daniel Veillard only very recently built V1.4a, and I 
don't think that he's released it yet (I've played with it a bit on my
resurrected system in the last day or two, and it seems to work fine).

Note that Amaya is intended more as an editor than a browser; it
generates very clean HTML and has lots of nice editing features, but
isn't the ideal tool for browsing.

It implements HTTP/1.1, and on faster networks, runs very fast indeed;
on dialup networks you may not appreciate things getting stuck behind
large images though.

See: http://www.w3.org/Amaya.
			- Jim



