I don't have my part number references here, but there are two variants
of the Multia riser card; one provides a PCI slot and SCSI interface,
with SCSI cabling running to an external HD50 port and a cable to connect
to an internal 2.5" SCSI disk, the other card provides
a SCSI interface with a single internal 50-pin connector for a 3.5" hard 
drive, but no PCI slot.  There is a separate bracket that mounts inside the
Multia to hold a 3.5" hard drive (SCSI) with this second riser.

Most folks recommend against running an internal 3.5" drive because of
internal heat problems and possibly pushing the limited power supply past
safe loading.  Do NOT try to run a 7200 RPM drive internally.  If you do
some shopping around you can find a slot cover adapter that has an internal
50 pin connector and an external HD5xx0 connector that allows you to bring
the internal SCSI to the outside world; works perfectly on mine (I have
one of each Multia)

As to your need for a second ethernet port... I'm far from up to date on
the state of Linux on the Multia, but aren't the PCMCIA slots supported?
Could you use a PCMCIA NIC for your purposes?

