In article <37131ce0.34122455@news.tc.umn.edu>,
	dang@cadif.cornell.edu (Dang H. Nguyen) writes:

> floppy drive with the Multia so I can boot Linux. However, the site
> seems to imply that if I get the model with the PCI riser card (needed
> if I want to install a second NIC for routing) then I won't be able to
> install a 3.5" HD internally. Is this true?

Yup.  With the PCI riser card, there won't be any room left over for
the 3.5" internal hard drive.  Your options are to use an external
drive or use a 2.5" drive internally.  An internal SCSI drive would be
your best bet, but the 2.5" ones are expensive.  I've heard varying
stories of success/failure using 2.5" IDE drives (which are certainly
cheaper).  

> I correct to assume that the PCI riser card model comes with external
> SCSI ports too?

You get an external SCSI port on the model with a PCI riser card.

