In article <37121C36.D6E71C1@cict.fr>, Georges Landa  <landa@cict.fr> wrote:
> Hi All,
>
> I have the following problem :
> I got some program, for example "grasp",  with the following attributes
> :
>
> -rwxr-xr-x   1 owner    group   3318022 Feb 16 09:46 grasp
>
> and when I want to launch it I get the following message :
>
> bash: ./grasp: No such file or directory
>
> As somebody an explanation ?

Based on the filesize, I'm going to get that it is a compiled binary of
some sort.  Otherwise, if it were a perl or shell script, check the first
line and make sure it points to an existing shell/perl call:

#!/usr/bin/perl

For example

If it is a compiled program, check to see what it is linked against with
ldd:

ldd ./grasp

The ldd run will show you what libs it it linked against and if ldd can
find the libs it needs.

-- 
Michael Parson
mparson@bl.org



