On Thu, 08 Apr 1999 04:17:44 GMT, Jeffrey Sturm <jsturm1@home.com> wrote:
>I don't know if this would be feasible... remember Alpha/NT is 32-bit...
>think how dosemu runs 16-bit apps, it requires special hardware support,
>called virtual-86 mode IIRC.

V86 mode is only required because the x86 differentiates between real
mode and protected mode.  The alpha has no "32-bit mode"; the NT
PALcode simply doesn't handle virtual addresses past 0xFFFFFFFF.

>Also, Alpha/NT runs under a completely different PALcode than Linux. 
>With these problems I don't know how object files could ever be shared
>between the two.

Since there are no conflicting unprivileged PALcode entry points, it's
not as big a problem as it may seem.  The NT-only calls should trap,
and can be emulated (although it's mostly stuff like "call kernel
debugger", which I don't think needs to be implemented. ;-))

The only possible problem I see is differing syscall formats, which use
the same PALcode entry point.  Hopefully they can be easily
differentiated by the kernel...

