Deja News was not working for a day or so, so I missed the original message
and some? of the answers...

You need to install the kernel source if it's not already. Then do a "make
config" do whatever you need for you setup and say yes to the experminatal
options. Say yes to most (all?) of the firewall, forwading, and masqurading.
After that do a "make dep ; make clean", then "make boot", copy vmlinux.gz to
/, then "make modules", and last "make modules install".

Get the ipfwadm SRPM for RH5.0 because the one for RH5.1 and 5.2 is broken.
do a "rpm -v --rebuild filename.rpm" (as root) to rebuild the package. You
then should have a binary RPM in /usr/src/redhat/RPMS/alpha after you do all
of that you need to install it with a "rpm -vU --oldpackage package.rpm", you
should then be in business!

If you using a 2.2.X kernel you need to upgrade serveral packages, see
redhat.com for more information.



