From: Steve.Lionel@compaq.com (Steve Lionel)
Subject: Compaq to port its Fortran and C compilers to Alpha Linux
Date: 1999/04/06
Message-ID: <371b3165.524614640@usenet.pa.dec.com>#1/1
X-Deja-AN: 463299471
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 7bit
Organization: Compaq Computer Corporation
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=us-ascii
Mime-Version: 1.0
Newsgroups: comp.lang.fortran,comp.lang.c,comp.os.linux.development,comp.os.linux.alpha

The following is an excerpt from a large Compaq press release (
http://www.compaq.com/newsroom/pr/1999/pr060499a.html) announced
today:

Linux and Tru64 UNIX Compatibility; Compaq Support

Compaq has now incorporated Linux into its enterprise UNIX strategy,
emphasizing its intentions to increase Linux and Tru64 UNIX
application and product compatibility. This will ensure a more
consistent, complete application platform for Linux customers. Compaq
will concentrate on Internet Service Providers (ISPs), High
Performance Technical Computing (HPTC) and Education as initial Linux
target markets.

Further establishing AlphaServers as the high performance leader in
Linux systems, and in direct response to demand from High Performance
Technical Computing customers, Compaq is also porting its Tru64 UNIX
Alpha Fortan and C compilers along with the associated runtime
libraries to Linux (Alpha) later this year. Additional
compilers/development tools will be considered as more requirements
are identified. Early testing has shown that the code generated by
Compaq Fortran for Linux on AlphaServers will perform floating point
calculations at least twice as fast as code generated by the g77
compiler for Linux on AlphaServers.

....

Our current thinking is that we'll have a "public beta" of the Fortran
compiler starting in July.  The C compiler will be somewhat later.
Please watch our web site (http://www.compaq.com/fortran) for more
details as they become available.


--
Steve Lionel (mailto:Steve.Lionel@compaq.com)
Fortran Engineering
Compaq Computer Corporation, Nashua NH

Compaq Fortran web site: http://www.compaq.com/fortran



