Not really ;)
It's not the fastest 533MHz Alpha but it works almost flawlessly by now. It
had some problems but as I said those are mostly gone now. The only bug I
see is that some programs using threads cause system instability (only
programs known to cause this so far: x11amp and mtvp).
Apart from this anything else is fine ;) If you want to use SCSI with it you
can start with a vanilla 2.2.* kernel (attention: up to 2.2.5 compile SCSI
CDROM into the kernel, not as module!). If you want to use IDE then you
might want to have a look at the IDE UDMA support. The 164SX's IDE chipset
is supported by now.

