In article <7e08s2$n2$1@freyja.bart.nl>,

> Get the AxPCI33 ("noname") board, it is cheap, you can put it in an old PC
> case, use most of your leftover PC hardware with it. and it can be upgraded
> from 166Mhz to 533Mhz. You must only be sure you can get parity SIMMs cheap
> and it doesn't work with all videocards.

The AXPpci33 CANNOT be upgraded to 533MHz! The AXPpci33 supports upto 300MHz
operation using 21066 generation processors. The fastest 21066 is 233MHz. The
300MHz+ Alphas are 21164 (or 21264) gernation processors. The Noname systems
are nice but old, if you want a more resent Alpha for the cheapest possible
price, I would recommend eBay auctions (computers.ebay.com, search for
"alpha") and look for a 21164 based system/motherboard.


Regards,

Ron Farrer

