Hello,
  This is a post on Mozilla and how I got it to run.

Lets face it Netscape bites. I am still using Netscape 3.04 because it was
the last one that was even near stable. So I decide to try out Mozilla.

First My system:

Redhat 5.2 / Kerenel 2.2.3 / 21164A @ 600 Mhz / Modem connection to net.

First I needed to install a bunch o packages. I found pointers to these on
http://rufus.w3.org

glib-1.2.1-1.alpha.rpm
glib-devel-1.2.1-1.alpha.rpm
glibc-2.1.1-1.alpha.rpm
gtk+-1.2.1-1.alpha.rpm
gtk+-devel-1.2.1-1.alpha.rpm

Then off of
ftp://ftp.alphalinux.org
I installed these packages:

binutils-2.9.1.0.22b-1.alpha.rpm
cpp-1.1.2-1.alpha.rpm
egcs-1.1.2-1.alpha.rpm
egcs-c++-1.1.2-1.alpha.rpm
egcs-g77-1.1.2-1.alpha.rpm
egcs-objc-1.1.2-1.alpha.rpm
libstdc++-2.9.0-1.alpha.rpm
procps-1.2.9-2.alpha.rpm
procps-X11-1.2.9-2.alpha.rpm

Then I went to:
ftp://ftp.mozilla.org/pub/mozilla/releases/m3/SRPMS/
and got

mozilla-5.0-SeaMonkey_M3_BRANCH_19990323.src.rpm
nspr-pthreads-3.1-SeaMonkey_M3_BRANCH_19990319.src.rpm

To compile:
Install all of the alpha packages.
perform an

rpm --rebuild nspr-pthreads-3.1-SeaMonkey_M3_BRANCH_19990319.src.rpm

then install it.

NOTE NOTE !!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!
The following link is need to compile mozilla:

cd /
ln -s /usr/src/redhat/builds

Mozilla has a mistake in the rpm.

Then install.


Reactions so far:
1. It seems really fast. Loading net pages pop (considering the modem)
   I also tryed my site. (local copy) And the pages just pop up.
2. Crashing. so far I have loaded 20 or so sites:
    http://www.cnn.com
    http://www.cs.rose-hulman.edu/~donaldlf
    http://www.slashdot.org
    http://www.alpha.linux.org

   I have crashed it by.
   1. Trying to load previous days information on slashdot.org. (bad url in
       page)
   2. Trying to cut and paste from the url locator.

3. Complaints:
  1. No mail/news reader (I think)
  2. Dosen't listen to my .gtkrc file ergo no theme support.
  3. Still a resource hog of 19 megs image size in memory however I haven't
     tried fine tuning the compile options yet. I know that assertions are
     and -g are still turned on.

4. It actually appears to be a usable beta release. Go forth and give it a
try.

Notes:
  1) I don't think you need glibc 2.1 but the gtk rpm were compiled with it.
  2) I should have recompiled everything with the
     gcc  -Wa,-mev56
    to (I think this works) make everything 21164 specific.
  3) So far I'm happy.


If anyone has any comments or questions feel free to drop me a line.

